\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7(0) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=T(13{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(13{v}_{1}) & =13T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =13[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad1c29f7-c0e7-5bed-944f-a2e33579c7b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using the Scalar Multiplication Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9748f047-caec-5d27-bbfe-fab439fc719a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262635} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c959bd-b3d1-5e97-8069-ecd792c039c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262636} {:answer/id #uuid "74710f2a-9370-54c1-8e25-8c251ada75c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262637} {:answer/id #uuid "8c06956e-c0b1-570d-9b6d-888d3b86cd7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262638} {:answer/id #uuid "63301b59-c472-5563-9947-977125bf95e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63301b59-c472-5563-9947-977125bf95e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262639} :answer-field/id #uuid "2527124d-1280-5c3f-8d85-046b339dfead" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af3683e8-195c-5b56-8022-1f63793fcbe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37870" :question/problem "If $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation and $\\,T([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $\\,T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]=4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]) & =T(4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])=4T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7fead9e-30c6-5f59-9993-b1e7f244ea5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085466} {:answer/id #uuid "ca948ea7-594b-5e5c-a292-8cdabb2b29cc" :ans